UID:f158ed8e495ea6e1@role-securities-financial.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260918T205252Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260918
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Protecting Maine Through Stronger Infrastruct
 ure and Climate Resiliency
DESCRIPTION:Hello\, this is Governor Janet Mills\, and thank you for liste
 ning.\nYou know\, when I took office nearly eight years ago\, I promised t
 hat Maine won't wait to take action to protect our state\, our people\, an
 d our economy from the dangers of extreme weather events caused by polluti
 on and changes to our environment. And I promised that we would fight to p
 reserve this special place that we call home\; preserve it for the benefit
  of our children and grandchildren.\nThe stakes could not be higher. Look 
 no further than the devastating storms of just a few years ago. Storms tha
 t impacted our communities\, our people\, and our economy—that destroyed
  a lot of infrastructure across the state.\nI've made climate action a cor
 nerstone of my Administration. First\, we created the Maine Climate Counci
 l\, and we issued a groundbreaking climate action plan. And we dedicated m
 illions of federal and state dollars to make that plan a reality.\nIn 2025
 \, we made the single largest investment in storm recovery by any administ
 ration in Maine history\, and we created the State Resilience Office to bu
 ild better\, stronger public infrastructure to withstand future storms.\nT
 hat office manages a partnership of more than 300 communities and has awar
 ded more than $29 million in state and federal funds for projects to prepa
 re local communities for flooding\, for storm surge\, for rising sea level
 s\, and other climate and weather events that put people's lives and livel
 ihoods at risk.\nRecently\, I was proud to announce the latest round of fu
 nding through that partnership:\nmore than $4.7 million in grants to 72 ci
 ties and Tribal Governments\n\, including the towns of Bingham and Madawas
 ka:\nThe Town of Bingham will install high-efficiency heat pumps and a roo
 ftop solar system in order to lower their energy costs at the municipally 
 owned Veterans Building\;\nThe Town of Madawaska will use their grant to l
 aunch the RIDER Program\, a shared e-bike fleet in a rural community that 
 doesn't have public transportation\;\nAnd the Tow\nhttp://www.maine.gov/go
 vernor/mills/news/radio_address/protecting-maine-through-stronger-infrastr
 ucture-and-climate-resiliency-2026-09
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/news/radio_address/protecting-main
 e-through-stronger-infrastructure-and-climate-resiliency-2026-09
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
